--- /dev/null
+++ b/COMPACT-500-VACUUM-SENSORS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,113 @@
+# Compact-500 vacuum sensor selection
+
+This branch supports either of these two -100..0 kPa vacuum sensors on both
+LumenPnP vacuum channels:
+
+| Strap at STM32 PE3 | Sensor | 7-bit I2C address |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| open / HIGH | CFSensor GZP6857D101KPN | `0x6D` |
+| GND / LOW | Haobang HBP1201D101GND6-4 | `0x58` |
+
+The selection is sampled at firmware startup. Changing the strap therefore
+requires a firmware restart. This keeps the sensor choice a simple, immutable
+hardware configuration during operation.
+
+## Motherboard wiring
+
+- STM32F407VET6 `PE3`, package pad 2, is unused on the stock REV05 schematic
+  and PCB.
+- Fit an external 10 kohm pull-up from PE3 to 3.3 V.
+- Fit a solder jumper or 0 ohm option from PE3 to GND.
+- Open selects the original GZP sensor. Closed selects the HBP replacement.
+- The firmware also enables the STM32 internal pull-up so an open input has a
+  defined level before or without the external resistor.
+
+The two sensors do not have the same power-pin arrangement. A universal PCB
+footprint must route pins 1 and 6 with assembly options appropriate to the
+selected sensor; firmware selection cannot compensate for incorrect power
+wiring.
+
+## Firmware interface
+
+Use the firmware command below instead of issuing raw `M260` / `M261`
+transactions from OpenPnP:
+
+```text
+M3427 T1
+M3427 T2
+```
+
+`T1` selects VAC1 / PCA9545A channel 0 and `T2` selects VAC2 / channel 1.
+For the HBP replacement, firmware startup automatically measures both channels
+with the pump and valve outputs initialized off, before any G-code can actuate
+them. It averages eight complete 24-bit samples per channel and stores the two
+ambient reference codes in RAM. Every power-up or reset repeats this step;
+OpenPnP needs no calibration command. If a channel cannot be sampled at boot,
+its reads return an error instead of inventing a zero. Keep the nozzles open
+during startup so the reference pressure is atmospheric. A successful read reports
+the gauge pressure and vacuum magnitude in pascals, a 0..255 legacy level
+(255 = ambient, 0 = -100 kPa), and the unchanged 24-bit sensor code:
+
+```text
+pressure_pa:-13124 vacuum_pa:13124 vacuum_level:222 raw_counts:655920 raw_bytes:10,2,48
+```
+
+The [HBP1201D-4 manufacturer datasheet](https://item.szlcsc.com/56393709.html)
+specifies I2C address 0x58, registers 0x04..0x06 and the transfer gain of
+100 kPa per 2^21 counts for this -100..0 kPa variant. Its formula includes a
+zero-point term but does not state that term's value for this exact part.
+The boot ambient reading supplies that missing term for each installed sensor.
+The first raw byte can therefore be 14 while gauge pressure is 0 kPa; the byte
+itself has no kPa unit. The original LumenPnP OpenPnP macro for its GZP sensor
+reads only register 0x06 as a relative level, without a kPa zero-point term.
+For HBP, `vacuum_level` is calculated from the full 24-bit pressure code after
+subtracting the boot reference: 255 at ambient and 0 at -100 kPa. The existing
+nozzle pickup thresholds still need to be checked with real parts.
+
+## Build
+
+Build the REV05 target with:
+
+```text
+pio run -e Opulo_Lumen_REV5
+```
+
+The DFU-suffixed image is generated at
+`.pio/build/Opulo_Lumen_REV5/firmware.bin`.
+
+### Compact-500 geometry and Apple Silicon build
+
+As configured on 2026-09-18, REV5 uses front-left X/Y MIN homing at (0, 0),
+with nominal travel X=333 mm and Y=387 mm. These are stock travel minus the
+100 mm frame reduction on each axis and require clearance verification.
+The HBP sensors in the KiCad BOM are selected by the fitted PE3-to-GND jumper;
+there is no forced sensor override. The existing Z settings remain.
+
+### Hardware bring-up status (2026-11-16)
+
+`INVERT_X_DIR` is now `false`. A full motor turn in each direction was tested
+on the machine and confirmed: positive X moves away from the X-MIN switch,
+negative X moves towards it. Z direction and switch detection were checked;
+positive Z moves down and negative Z moves up towards Z-MIN.
+
+Both ring lights passed the RGB test with the original repository NeoPixel
+sender after a defective level shifter was replaced. The temporary custom
+timing sender and white-at-25-percent boot preset were removed. The original
+startup color test followed by lights off is retained.
+
+An isolated slow Z reference test passed. The full `G28 Z` sequence still
+requires X/Y homing because `Z_SAFE_HOMING` remains enabled; the test with
+disconnected X/Y stopped with `Homing Failed`. No slow-homing firmware changes
+were retained.
+
+On this Apple Silicon host, use:
+
+```sh
+/Users/julius/.platformio/penv/bin/python -m platformio run \
+  -c platformio-macos-arm64.ini -e Opulo_Lumen_REV5
+```
+
+This pins the existing Arduino STM32 framework and native GCC 10.3.1, and
+uses locally compiled dfu-util 0.11 from `../.tools/dfu-native`. Its libusb
+dependency currently comes from the installed ARM FreeCAD application.
+The standard build configuration is retained for other hosts.
